  "body": "Thanks for the bug reports.  This is another bugfix release for the v0.14.x series, done primarily to fix a [CVE](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-110237).  The other backported changes since v0.14.4 make documentation more complete and readable along with fixing various bugs.\r\n\r\nThe CVE may allow a local user of a Unix-like system to send commands to a Vifm instance of another user.  Making `$TMPDIR`, `$TEMP`, `$TEMPDIR` or `$TMP` point at a location that's writable only by the current user is enough to make it impossible, but it needs to be done outside of Vifm (i.e., don't put `let $TMPDIR = ...` to `vifmrc`, it won't have the desired effect).\r\n\r\n[More details](https://vifm.info/v0.14.5)\r\n",
